165	 * Merging a person into another on the same sheet. Only a steward may; merging a person into themselves, or
166	 * when either of them is retired, is refused. The merged person's claims move to the other (numbers and dates
167	 * kept, listed after the other's claims in the order they were added, each keeping any figure a statement
168	 * bound); their statements are carried to the other, who keeps their own last statement (or, having none,
169	 * takes the merged person's last) with the count of both; their name and aliases become the other's aliases; their patrons are added to the
170	 * other's (never the other themselves, no repeats); anyone naming them as patron names the other instead
171	 * (no repeats); their pool memberships move to the other, the shares added up (at most 100.00) where the
172	 * other is already a member. Their holds, watchers and contact are dropped with them.
173	 */
