 33	/**
 34	 * The pools on a sheet, sorted by name, and their members: people of the sheet, each in a pool at most once, or
 35	 * other pools of the sheet, each a member of at most one pool, with a share percent. A pool cannot contain itself
 36	 * through any chain of pools, and a chain is at most three pools deep. A pool's total share counts every member's share,
 37	 * a retired member's (a retirement date set, whatever the date) as given; the pool is balanced when its total is
 38	 * exactly 100.00.
 39	 * A pool that is a member of none has the sheet's pot; a pool that is a member of another has as its pot its cut in
 40	 * that pool (none when that pool has no cuts). Each member of a balanced pool with a pot has a cut: 0.00 for a
 41	 * retired member or a person with a hold covering the sheet's today, otherwise the pot times their share divided by
 42	 * the shares of the members with a cut added up, rounded half to even to two decimals; the remainder, the pot less
 43	 * the cuts added up, goes to the member with the smallest non-zero cut, the latest added on a tie (to the last member
 44	 * with a cut and a share when no cut is non-zero), so the cuts total exactly the pot (all 0.00 when no member has a cut, but none at all when every member is retired). A hold
 45	 * changes neither the total share nor the balance.
 46	 * A membership may be dated, from and to (both days included, either open); a member whose dates do not include the
 47	 * sheet's today is left out entirely: not in the total share nor the balance, and no cut (shown, with its share).
 48	 * Every crew is also a pool under its name, listed with the stored pools: its lead and then its members, undated, at
 49	 * equal shares of 100.00 (each rounded half to even, the remainder on the lead), cut from the sheet's pot like any
 50	 * pool. Its members come from the crew, so none can be added to it here, and a pool cannot take a crew's name.
 51	 * For every period whose to-date is on or before the sheet's today, each member has the cut they had as the sheet
 52	 * stood at the end of that period (its pools, members, pot and holds then, that day as its today); none when they
 53	 * had none then.
 54	 */
